Example: Atomic Radial Wavefunction Calculation
===============================================

This example demonstrates the generation of relativistic radial wavefunctions
for an atomic system using RWFS. The program supports several central
potentials, including

  (a) Coulomb (unscreened),
  (b) Thomas–Fermi,
  (c) Multi-Yukawa.

The same procedure applies to neutral atoms, ions, or user-defined
electronic configurations.

1. Input Preparation
--------------------

Prepare an input file (e.g. input.dat) containing

  • Atomic number (Z)
  • Number of electrons (Ne)
  • List of orbitals in spectroscopic notation, for example

      1s 2s 2p- 2p
      3s 3p- 3p 3d- 3d
      4s 4p- 4p ...

  • Choice of central potential

      1 : Thomas–Fermi
      2 : Coulomb (unscreened)
      3 : Multi-Yukawa

For the Multi-Yukawa potential, the required screening parameters are
specified automatically from the internal database.

2. Run the Calculation
----------------------

Execute RWFS using

    python /path/to/rwfs.py < input.dat > output.out

or equivalently

    python rwfs.py < input.dat > output.out

depending on the installation.

3. Program Output
-----------------

After successful execution, RWFS prints a summary of the calculation,
including

  • atomic number and number of electrons,
  • selected central potential,
  • orbital energies (a.u. and eV),
  • expectation values ⟨r⟩ and ⟨r²⟩,
  • radial mesh information,
  • convergence status for each orbital.

A typical summary is

Orbital    n   κ        E (a.u.)      E (eV)      <r>      <r²>     NP
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
1s         1  -1      ...
2s         2  -1      ...
2p-        2   1      ...
2p         2  -2      ...
...
ns         n  -1      ...

Only converged orbitals are included in the summary table. If convergence
fails for any requested orbital, it is reported separately at the end of
the calculation.

4. Output Files
---------------

RWFS produces several output files depending on the selected options.

radial.rwf
    Radial wavefunctions in ASCII format.

grasp_*
    Orbitals written in a format compatible with the GRASP package.

summary.dat
    Orbital energies and radial expectation values.

potential_*
    Radial central potential used in the calculation.

Additional files may be generated depending on the selected output options.
